                <pb facs="0625" n="513" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg513"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 24199/11.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Bailly-Blanchard to the Secretary of
                            State</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1910-07-08"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">July 8,
                    1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the instruction of the
                    department of April 18, 1910 (serial No. 58), in regard to the presentation by
                    the people of Virginia to the people of France of a reproduction in bronze of
                    the statue of George Washington, made by Jean Antoine Houdon, I have the honor
                    to transmit herewith a copy and translation of the reply of M. Pichon, minister
                    of foreign affairs, to the note I addressed to mm on the subject.</p>
                <p>As you will observe, M. Pichon informs me that the statute is to be placed at
                    Versailles, and that the date for the inauguration has been fixed for the 18th
                    of August next, and further that this date will enable M. Jusserand to be
                    present at the ceremony.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A.
                    Bailly–Blanchard.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d590-a1.xml" xpointer="d590-a1"/>
            </div>
